ltsp (6.3.20-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * init-ltsp.d/50-console-font loads CONSOLE_FONT once per virtual
    terminal, the way console-setup's own cached script does, instead of
    once on whatever console setfont happens to open. In init-ltsp that
    is whatever init handed us for stdin, which need not be the terminal
    the boot messages appear on - so the font could be loaded somewhere
    nobody was looking. The fallback path already did it per terminal;
    only the CONSOLE_FONT branch did not.
  * doc/PXE-network-boot-test records iPXE's "could not open
    autoexec.ipxe" message as harmless. It is iPXE's own autoexec
    feature looking on the filesystem it booted from, which a network
    boot does not have; a file in the TFTP root does not silence it,
    because the URI scheme is file: and not tftp:.

