ltsp (6.3.16-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The documentation that had not been touched since LTSP 5 is rewritten.

    QuickInstall described installing ltsp-server-standalone on Ubuntu and
    running ltsp-build-client with no arguments - a package that does not
    exist here and an invocation that would not produce a usable image. It
    is now one server and one client on Debian 13, in six steps, each of
    which has been checked against what the tools actually do. Among other
    things it no longer tells the reader to run "ltsp-config dhcpd", which
    ltsp-config has never accepted: the argument is isc-dhcp-server.

    The FAQ answered questions about LTSP 4 versus 5, i386 chroot paths,
    inittab conflicts and a MueKow wiki that has not existed for fifteen
    years. It is now sorted by symptom - what you see, since at the point
    of asking the cause is what you do not know - and each entry says where
    the full account lives.

    TODO was the upstream wishlist from 2007. What it holds now is the one
    thing this project has genuinely left open: choosing a session server
    by what it has free, rather than by connection count.

  * README.md and README.de.md: the package table said 6.0.0-4 and 3.0.2-1,
    which is eleven releases ago. Both now also list the manual pages, which
    are the reference and were not mentioned at all, and show the
    ltsp-build-client invocation that produces a working image. The English
    README had a German section heading.

